        "synthesis": {
          "model_calls": 1,
          "phase": "synthesis",
          "plan": {
            "A": "Research the sparse-obstacle path-counting approach: sort and deduplicate blocked coordinates, use modular binomial counts with inclusion-exclusion when its measured cost is competitive, and retain a correct dense or rolling-DP fallback otherwise. Tune any crossover from measured costs rather than assumed obstacle patterns. Validate blocked start/destination, duplicates, and all valid dimensions; do not specialize to the supplied cases.",
            "B": "Refine the measured anti-diagonal recurrence, currently the fastest candidate at 0.00816 s versus the 0.07927 s baseline. Preserve the dependency-free interior updates and explicit boundary/blocked-cell handling; investigate safe ARM64/GCC vectorization and whether parallel work pays off on the 4-core target. Measure any change independently and verify correctness before retaining it.",
            "C": "Investigate the rolling-row recurrence with obstacle lists and segmented parallel scans as a low-memory alternative. The current measured version is 0.03553 s; assess the serial/parallel crossover and scan overhead on the 4-core target, while preserving left/top dependencies and blocked-cell resets. Keep the algorithm general and validate it across the full valid input range.",
            "G": "Integrate and benchmark complete candidate programs rather than assuming gains combine. Use the anti-diagonal candidate as the current performance reference, but retest every integrated version for correctness and runtime; compare against the baseline and retain the best measured correct result. Avoid mixing incompatible recurrences or adding unmeasured changes, and do not change tests, oracle, compiler, budgets, target, permissions, or source outside the assigned integration work.",
            "analysis": "The source performs an O(N²) grid recurrence and allocates an O(N²) blocked-cell structure, which is a central cost for the stated large dimensions. On the ARM64 4-core, no-GPU target, the supplied measurements favor B's anti-diagonal recurrence at 0.00816 s; C's rolling-row scan measured 0.03553 s, while the row-major rolling-DP and sparse hybrid measured about 0.049 s each. The bitmap-only and sparse parallel inclusion-exclusion candidates were slower than baseline. These results justify distinct research lanes and a measured integration decision, not assuming transformations are additive or that one candidate wins on every valid input."
          },
